---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SupportState from '../components/SupportState.astro';
import { PROJECT } from '../content/wording';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Bridging the Laptop-to-Cluster Gap"
  description="Public BSSw Fellowship guidance for translating multi-service laptop workflows to scheduler-managed HPC systems."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <h1>Bridging the Laptop-to-Cluster Gap</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    A multi-service stack is trivial to run with Docker Compose on a laptop. On a shared
    cluster there is no Docker daemon, and the scheduler owns every resource. This guide is
    the translation — for scientific software practitioners, HPC learners, and workflow maintainers.
    No account is required to read anything here.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="mapping">
    <h2 id="mapping">What changes</h2>
    <dl class="mapping">
      <div>
        <dt><code>service</code></dt>
        <dd>Scheduler job or step</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><code>depends_on</code></dt>
        <dd>Explicit readiness check</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><code>volumes</code></dt>
        <dd>Job-scoped scratch</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><code>ports</code></dt>
        <dd>Loopback, reached by tunnel</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="mapping-note">
      <a href="/guide/scheduler-as-orchestrator/">The full mapping, and why each one shifts</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="path">
    <h2 id="path">Start here</h2>
    <ol class="path">
      <li>
        <h3><a href="/guide/scheduler-as-orchestrator/">Understand the model</a></h3>
        <p>How a scheduler allocation replaces Compose as the orchestration boundary.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="/start/">Check your center</a></h3>
        <p>Prerequisites, assumptions, and the values that differ at every site.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="/guide/baseline-single-node-pattern/">Run the baseline</a></h3>
        <p>
          A coordinator, a readiness gate, workers, and result verification in one allocation.
          Validated on Purdue Anvil (Slurm 25.11.1, Apptainer 1.4.3).
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="release-link">
      Current release: <strong>{PROJECT.release}</strong>. <a href="/releases/v0-1-0/">Release status</a> · <a href="/milestones/1/">Milestone 1 deliverables</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="browse">
    Browse the <a href="/resources/">resource index</a>,
    the <a href="/diagnostics/">diagnostic registry</a>,
    every <a href="/milestones/1/">Milestone 1 deliverable</a>,
    or the <a href={PROJECT.repository}>companion repository</a>.
  </p>

  <SupportState />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The mapping is the page's thesis, so it gets the one piece of visual weight
     the rest of the design deliberately withholds. */
  .mapping {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    border-top: 0.15rem solid #172033;
  }
  .mapping > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, auto) 1fr;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #c6ccd6;
  }
  .mapping dt {
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .mapping dt code {
    background: #f2f4f8;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
  }
  .mapping dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Direction of translation, without relying on colour or an image. */
  .mapping dd::before {
    content: "→ ";
    color: #596579;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .mapping-note {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .path {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .path > li {
    counter-increment: step;
    border-top: 0.15rem solid #0759a5;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .path > li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    display: block;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: #596579;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .path h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .path p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .release-link {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
  }

  .browse {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .mapping > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
